.TH CYAML_SET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cyaml_set \- write a C scalar to the DOM leaf addressed by a path
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t cyaml_set(cyaml root, const char *path, val);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Detect the compile-time type of val via _Generic and call
_cyaml_set_typed() to write a scalar value to the leaf node addressed
by path.

Accepted C types for val and the resulting CYAML node type:
  bool                      -> CYAML_BOOL
  any integer type          -> CYAML_INTEGER (stored as long long)
  float / double            -> CYAML_FLOAT (stored as double)
  char * / const char *     -> CYAML_STRING (heap copy made)
  string literal ("...")    -> CYAML_STRING
  a bare NULL literal       -> CYAML_NULL

Any other C type (long double, a struct, an enum, or any pointer
type other than char * / const char *) is rejected: cyaml_set
returns ccol_invalid_args and the target leaf is left untouched
(created leaves are not left behind as CYAML_NULL for an unsupported
type; an existing leaf's value is not overwritten).

A char[N] ARRAY VARIABLE (as opposed to a string literal written
directly at the call site) cannot be passed directly; cast it to
(char *) first.  This is a plain C language restriction (the macro
copies val into a same-typed local, which is not possible for a
non-literal array), not a cyaml-specific one.

For a dictionary leaf, the key is created when absent; its immediate
parent dictionary must already exist.  For a list leaf ("#N"), the
index must already be in range; a list has no way to be
auto-extended to fit an arbitrary index.  Either way, if the leaf
exists its type is replaced unconditionally: existing list or
dictionary subtrees are deep-freed before the new value is written.

Non-finite doubles (Inf, -Inf, NaN) are accepted and stored (unlike
cyaml_set on a cjson DOM).  They serialize as .inf, -.inf, .nan.

Passing (bool)true / (bool)false is required to produce a CYAML_BOOL
node; without the explicit cast, integer literal 1 or 0 produces a
CYAML_INTEGER node instead.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
root   Root cyaml handle.
path   Dot-separated path string.
       Escape sequences: '\e.' -> literal '.', '\e\e' -> literal '\e'.
       A '\e' before any other character is left unchanged.
val    C value; type is resolved at compile time.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_retval_t: ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args; empty path, type incompatible at a path step,
                      malformed "#N" list-index syntax, an empty path
                      component (nothing between two dots, or a
                      leading or trailing dot), or val's C type is
                      not one of the accepted types listed above.
ccol_key_not_found; a non-leaf component of the path does not exist,
                      or a leaf "#N" list index is syntactically
                      valid but out of range.
ccol_not_enough_memory; allocation failure.
ccol_container_full; creating a new leaf dictionary key would exceed
                      the parent's maximum representable element
                      count (not reachable in practice).
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cyaml_set(doc, "server.port",  8080);
cyaml_set(doc, "server.name",  "prod");
cyaml_set(doc, "server.tls",   (bool)true);
cyaml_set(doc, "server.ratio", 0.95);

/* Replace a dictionary subtree with a scalar */
cyaml_set(doc, "server.options", 0);   /* deep-frees old subtree */

/* Set to null */
cyaml_set(doc, "server.deprecated", NULL);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_get (3),
.BR _cyaml_set_typed (3)
